# CA Saathi — Cline Rules

# Read this file before every single task## What we are building

CA Saathi is an AI-powered practice management SaaS platform for Indian Chartered Accountants. It has two parts:

1. A web app (Next.js 14) for the CA to manage their practice
2. A client portal (PWA) for the CA's clients to upload documents and check filing status

## Tech stack — use exactly these, nothing else

- Frontend: Next.js 14 with App Router, TypeScript (strict mode), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
- Backend: Next.js API routes (same project)
- Database: PostgreSQL via Prisma ORM (hosted on Supabase)
- Job queue: BullMQ with Redis (hosted on Upstash)
- File storage: Cloudflare R2 (S3-compatible)
- AI engine: Anthropic Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-6)
- Email: Resend
- SMS (OTP only): Fast2SMS
- Payments: Razorpay
- Push notifications: Web Push API with VAPID keys

## Folder structure rules

- All pages go in: src/app/(dashboard)/ or src/app/(auth)/ or src/app/(client-portal)/- All API routes go in: src/app/api/
- All reusable components go in: src/components/
- All backend utilities go in: src/lib/
- All background workers go in: workers/
- Database schema is in: prisma/schema.prisma

## Coding rules — follow these always

1. Every database query that fetches by ID MUST include firm_id in the WHERE clause — no exceptions
2. Never hard delete anything — always use deleted_at for soft deletes
3. Never call Claude API directly from an API route — always queue a BullMQ job first
4. Never handle file bytes on the server — always use pre-signed R2 URLs for upload and download5. All AI outputs must have review_status = DRAFT until CA explicitly marks them reviewed6. Every webhook endpoint must validate the signature before processing anything
5. PAN numbers must be encrypted using AES-256-GCM before storing in database
6. Use ok(), err(), created() helpers from src/lib/utils/api.ts for all API responses
7. Use Zod for validating every API input
8. TypeScript strict mode — no 'any' types allowed

## API response format — always use thisimport { ok, err } from ''lib/utils/api'' (see below for file content)

return ok(data) // for success
return err('message') // for errors

## The three MVP features (most important)

1. Notice AI — CA uploads notice PDF → AI reads it → drafts legal reply → CA reviews → downloads PDF
2. GST Reconciliation — CA uploads GSTR-2B + purchase register → AI matches → shows mismatches
3. Client Portal — clients register with phone OTP → set PIN → use biometric → upload documents

## Security rules — never break these

- Every API route reads firm_id from the JWT header x-firm-id set by middleware
- Firm A can never see Firm B's data — enforced at both API and database level
- JWTs stored in httpOnly cookies on web — never in localStorage
- Webhook signatures validated using HMAC before any processing
